On Nov 27 Premier Li Qiang chaired a State Council executive meeting that set out capital-market measures:

- improve market-stabilisation mechanisms, carry out existing policies and plan new ones;
- push listed companies to raise dividends and buybacks;
- strengthen the 'national team', with Central Huijin acting as a quasi-stabilisation fund backed by liquidity support;
- steer insurers, annuities and social-security funds into equities, and guard against external shocks.

After the rare midday release, A-shares rallied across the board. The Shanghai Composite reclaimed 3,600, closing 3.73% higher at 3,606.49, its biggest one-day gain in two years. ChiNext rose 11.61% and the STAR Composite 14.21%, led by the semiconductor supply chain.

Sources: [gov.cn](https://www.gov.cn/yaowen/liebiao/202611/content_7087445.htm), [Xinhua](https://english.news.cn/20261127/cc3749512b134b3aa6a653dd558e9621/c.html), [Bloomberg](https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-27/china-s-cabinet-stresses-market-support-in-midday-release), [Lianhe Zaobao](https://www.zaobao.com.sg/news/china/story20261127-10067085)
